#!/usr/bin/env bun
// Voice prebuild: counts the texts in villagers, packs, modules, scenarios, scenes, «Vidim, vidim» (what a child says
// playing I spy in the scenes: companion/ispy), the keepers' talks (the culture's spots: the charcoal burner's meeting and
// his story), the village projects' steps (the culture's project-steps/), the storyteller's stories and the car's drills (Slovene, or the
// language of the learner's culture pack, LANI_CULTURE, with its own voice cast), what is voiced, what is missing and
// the ElevenLabs quota left. With --run, generates the missing clips in priority order (villager lines in their
// speakers' voices, pack words, examples, modules, scenarios, the stories' tellings at A1, the drills at A1, scenes,
// the keepers' talks and the projects' steps, I spy's lines (in the voice of each child who may play there), then the tellings at A2, the drills
// above A1, the tellings at B1 and up; a telling and a
// riddle in the teller's voice, their own designed one where it is ready ("@janez": ElevenLabs only), a drill's other
// texts in the narrator's: the car plays a story or a drill's item only when its clips exist):
// ElevenLabs down to the reserve, then the local worker (not for a villager line whose narrator clip
// exists: the app plays that one until ElevenLabs makes theirs).
//
// In a Slovene village the narrators (female, male) speak with the local Gepard voice (nina, marko), never the English
// library voices (README, "Voice"); elsewhere a narrator says a short text (1–3 words) inside a carrier sentence, which is
// cut out, and the plan shows how many narrator words are still old-style (said plainly) and what re-voicing them costs.
//
// Usage: companion/bin/voice-build [--run] [--upgrade] [--revoice speaker[,speaker]] [--max-chars N] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --revoice-words [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --denoise [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --level [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --edges [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --tempo [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard SNAPSHOT [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//        companion/bin/voice-build --narrators [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]
//   --upgrade        also replace local (Gepard) clips with ElevenLabs ones while the quota lasts
//   --revoice S      make every clip of speaker S again with ElevenLabs (after swapping its voice in companion/voice-cast.json)
//   --max-chars N    spend at most N ElevenLabs characters in this run
//   --revoice-words  only the old-style short narrator words again, in their carrier sentence, most asked for first,
//                    at most --max N of them, within the reserve (the bridge does this lazily, a few a day)
//   --denoise        the clips of the voices the cast marks "denoise" (a voice that hisses) through their filter, those
//                    not filtered yet (the bridge filters new ones as it stores them), at most --max N; each under a new
//                    file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded. Levelled in the same encode.
//   --level          every clip not at the level yet (one loudness, LEVEL in bridge/src/voice.ts: −18 LUFS, true peak
//                    at most −1.5 dBTP; the bridge levels new clips as it stores them), oldest first, at most --max N.
//                    The dry run measures them and shows each voice's loudness before and the gain. A clip is levelled
//                    once: its row records the target (level) and the gain; after a change of the target, --level
//                    levels the clips again from their files as they are (one more encode; a clip within 0.5 dB of the
//                    target keeps its file). A clip whose voice's filter is due is filtered in the same encode. Each
//                    under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded; a running bridge tells
//                    the app within a minute (voice_updated).
//   --edges          every clip whose silence at the edges isn't trimmed yet (EDGES in bridge/src/voice.ts: 0.05 s kept
//                    before the sound, 0.1 s after it; the bridge trims new clips as it stores them), of every engine,
//                    oldest first, at most --max N. The dry run measures them: per engine, how many have more than
//                    0.1 s of silence before the sound or 0.2 s after it (twice what is kept), and the silence now and
//                    after. --run trims those, levelled again in the same encode, each under a new file name, the old
//                    file removed once the new one is recorded; the others are only recorded (edges), so no clip is
//                    done twice.
//   --tempo          only with a pace set (LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_TEMPO, a factor; LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_PAUSES, the longest
//                    pause kept; neither by default: the local voice keeps its own pace): the local (Gepard) clips not
//                    at it yet, at most --max N; the dry run measures each clip's characters a second now and as it
//                    would be paced. Levelled again in the same encode, under a new file name.
//                    --denoise, --level, --edges and --tempo use ffmpeg only: no ElevenLabs, no characters.
//   --restore-gepard SNAPSHOT
//                    the local clips paced before (tempo set: October 2026's ×1.05 pass) back to their files and rows in
//                    SNAPSHOT, a lani-backup snapshot taken before that (its voice/, or a voice store's directory: voice.db
//                    and files/; read only, its database from a copy). The dry run lists what it would restore and what
//                    it can't; --run copies each file back (checked byte for byte), points the row at it with the
//                    snapshot's level and gain, and removes the paced file once the row is moved. Then --edges trims them.
//   --narrators      in a Slovene village: the narrators' clips (female, male) not in their local voice yet (nina,
//                    marko: ElevenLabs' English narrators, the female narrator's ana) made again by the local worker,
//                    most asked for first, at most --max N, one at a time (about a second each). Only Slovene texts: a
//                    clip of this village's corpus, of a source the corpus has (a pack, a scene, …), or a line the app
//                    spoke here (live, road); the dry run lists the others, which stay as they are. The edges trimmed
//                    and levelled as every new clip; a worker that is down stops the run, and the next run goes on.
//   --data DIR       the learner data directory, as LANI_DATA_DIR (a copy; another learner's profiles/<id>/data with
//                    their LANI_CULTURE)
// Without --run, a dry run. The key comes from ELEVENLABS_API_KEY, else ~/.config/lani/keys.env (LANI_KEYS_FILE).
import '../bridge/src/env' // first: LANI_* from the FLUENT_* names of a node set up before the rename
import { existsSync, readFileSync, statSync } from 'node:fs'
import { join, resolve } from 'node:path'
import { addresseeOf } from '../bridge/src/addressee'
import { cast, castVoiced, denoiseVoices, isSpeaker, personVoice, useCastFile, usePersonVoices } from '../bridge/src/cast'
import { ownVoicesIn } from '../bridge/src/profiles'
import { cultureDir, cultureKeepers, keeperTellings, resolveCulture } from '../bridge/src/cultures'
import { cultureStepFiles, stepTellings } from '../bridge/src/project-steps'
import { DrillStore, drillsDir } from '../bridge/src/drills'
import { grammarDir, GrammarStore } from '../bridge/src/grammar'
import { readISpy } from '../bridge/src/ispy'
import { ModuleStore } from '../bridge/src/store'
import { PackStore, packsDirs } from '../bridge/src/packs'
import { ScenarioStore } from '../bridge/src/scenarios'
import { SceneStore, scenesDirs } from '../bridge/src/scenes'
import { StoryStore, storiesDirs } from '../bridge/src/stories'
import { VillagerStore } from '../bridge/src/villagers'
import { cardTexts, charsPerSecond, clipKey, corpus, EDGES, enginesFromEnv, ffmpegDenoiser, ffmpegFileEdges, ffmpegLeveller, ffmpegLoudness, ffmpegPace, FILE, LEVEL, levelGain, LIMIT_MARGIN, localNarrators, paceChain, trimmable, VoiceStore, type Clip, type Edges, type Loudness, type Pace } from '../bridge/src/voice'
import { formatPlan, plan, run } from '../bridge/src/prebuild'
import { normalizeText } from '../bridge/src/family'
import { keysFile } from '../bridge/src/env'
import { voiceDir } from '../bridge/src/paths'
import { setting } from '../bridge/src/env'

const root = resolve(import.meta.dir, '../..')
// the learner's village's culture pack (LANI_CULTURE, as their bridge has it; primorska by default): its language,
// its cast, its voice cast, its packs and its own scenes
const cultures = process.env.LANI_CULTURES_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/cultures')
// (lani.env's for the default learner; another --data directory's comes from LANI_CULTURE in the environment only)
const dataArg = process.argv.indexOf('--data') >= 0 ? process.argv[process.argv.indexOf('--data') + 1] : undefined
const village = resolveCulture(cultures, setting('LANI_CULTURE', dataArg ? { ...process.env, LANI_DATA_DIR: resolve(dataArg) } : process.env))
const culture = village.id
const language = village.manifest?.language ?? 'sl'
// the curated content of the village's language (a subdirectory for another than Slovene, as the bridge has it)
const ofLanguage = (dir: string) => (language === 'sl' ? dir : join(dir, language))
const castFile = join(cultureDir(cultures, culture), 'voice-cast.json')
if (existsSync(castFile)) useCastFile(castFile)

const args = process.argv.slice(2)
const flag = (f: string) => args.includes(f)
const maxAt = args.indexOf('--max-chars')
const maxChars = maxAt >= 0 ? Number(args[maxAt + 1]) : undefined
const revAt = args.indexOf('--revoice')
const revoice = revAt >= 0 ? (args[revAt + 1] ?? '').split(',').filter(Boolean) : []
const unknown = revoice.filter(s => !isSpeaker(s))
const revoiceWords = flag('--revoice-words')
const denoise = flag('--denoise')
const level = flag('--level')
const tempo = flag('--tempo')
const edges = flag('--edges')
const narrators = flag('--narrators')
const restoreAt = args.indexOf('--restore-gepard')
const snapshotArg = restoreAt >= 0 ? args[restoreAt + 1] : undefined
// a lani-backup snapshot (its voice/), or a voice store's own directory (voice.db and files/)
const snapshot = snapshotArg ? [join(snapshotArg, 'voice'), snapshotArg].find(d => existsSync(join(d, 'voice.db')) && existsSync(join(d, 'files'))) : undefined
const badSnapshot = restoreAt >= 0 && !snapshot
const restore = restoreAt >= 0
const maxAt2 = args.indexOf('--max')
const max = maxAt2 >= 0 ? Number(args[maxAt2 + 1]) : undefined
const badMax = max !== undefined && !(Number.isInteger(max) && max >= 0)
const dataAt = args.indexOf('--data')
const data = dataAt >= 0 ? args[dataAt + 1] : undefined
const badData = dataAt >= 0 && !(data && existsSync(data) && statSync(data).isDirectory())
const modes = [revoiceWords, denoise, level, tempo, edges, restore, narrators, revAt >= 0 || flag('--upgrade')].filter(Boolean).length
const ffmpegOnly = denoise || level || tempo || edges || restore || narrators
if (flag('--help') || flag('-h') || (maxChars !== undefined && !(maxChars >= 0)) || (revAt >= 0 && !revoice.length) || unknown.length || badMax || badData || badSnapshot || (maxAt2 >= 0 && !revoiceWords && !ffmpegOnly) || modes > 1 || (ffmpegOnly && maxAt >= 0)) {
  if (unknown.length) console.error(`not in the voice cast: ${unknown.join(', ')} (the cast: ${Object.keys(cast()).join(', ')})`)
  if (badData) console.error(`--data: no directory ${data ?? ''}`)
  if (badSnapshot) console.error(`--restore-gepard: no voice store (voice.db and files/) in ${snapshotArg ?? '(none given)'} or its voice/`)
  console.log('Usage: companion/bin/voice-build [--run] [--upgrade] [--revoice speaker[,speaker]] [--max-chars N] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --revoice-words [--max N] [--max-chars N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --denoise [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --level [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --edges [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --tempo [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard SNAPSHOT [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  console.log('       companion/bin/voice-build --narrators [--max N] [--run] [--json] [--data DIR]')
  process.exit(flag('--help') || flag('-h') ? 0 : 2)
}
// the data directory the clips are in (ensure_data_dir.py reads LANI_DATA_DIR)
if (data) process.env.LANI_DATA_DIR = resolve(data)

// The key file holds KEY=value lines; only what isn't already in the environment is taken.
const keys = keysFile()
if (existsSync(keys)) {
  for (const line of readFileSync(keys, 'utf8').split('\n')) {
    const m = /^\s*(?:export\s+)?([A-Z_][A-Z0-9_]*)\s*=\s*(.*?)\s*$/.exec(line)
    if (m && process.env[m[1]] === undefined) process.env[m[1]] = m[2].replace(/^(['"])(.*)\1$/, '$2')
  }
}

const p = Bun.spawnSync(['python3', '.claude/hooks/ensure_data_dir.py'], { cwd: root, env: { ...process.env, CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR: root } })
if (p.exitCode !== 0) throw new Error(`ensure_data_dir.py failed: ${p.stderr.toString()}`)
const appDir = join(p.stdout.toString().trim(), 'app')
// the clips: the voice cache ($LANI_VOICE_CACHE, lani.env's for the default learner), else <data>/app/voice

const log = (...a: unknown[]) => console.error('[voice-build]', ...a)
// the store as the bridge has it: the narrators of a Slovene village in the local voice (LANI_VOICE_NARRATOR_SL)
const villageVoices = { language, localNarrators: localNarrators(language, process.env, log) }

if (denoise) {
  // the clips of the voices that hiss, through their filter: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const voices = denoiseVoices()
  const queue = store.denoiseQueue()
  const summary = { voices, waiting: queue.length, stats: store.denoiseStats(), dir: store.dir }
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, clips: queue.slice(0, max).map(c => ({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, file: c.file, preset: c.preset, text: c.text })) }, null, 2))
    else {
      console.log(`Voices filtered (the cast's "denoise"): ${Object.entries(voices).map(([v, p]) => `${v} (${p})`).join(', ') || 'none'}`)
      console.log(`Clips in ${store.dir} waiting for their filter: ${queue.length}${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
      for (const c of queue.slice(0, max)) console.log(`  ${c.preset.padEnd(11)} ${c.voice.padEnd(10)} ${c.file}  ${c.text.length > 64 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 63)}…` : c.text}`)
      console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each would be filtered with ffmpeg${summary.stats.ffmpeg ? '' : ' (not found here: LANI_FFMPEG)'} and brought to the level in the same encode, and stored under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded.`)
      console.log(`Filter with: companion/bin/voice-build --denoise --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    }
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegDenoiser()) {
    console.error('voice-build --denoise: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Filtering ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s) …`)
  const r = await store.denoiseClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nFiltered ${r.done} clip(s)${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (level) {
  // every clip at one loudness: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const queue = store.levelQueue()
  const target = store.levelTarget
  const tail = `${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    // each clip measured as it would be levelled (through its voice's filter and a local clip's pace when they are due):
    // nothing is written
    const measure = ffmpegLoudness()
    const voices = denoiseVoices()
    const factor = store.pace
    const list = queue.slice(0, max)
    if (!measure) console.error('voice-build --level: no ffmpeg here (LANI_FFMPEG names one): nothing measured')
    else if (list.length) console.error(`Measuring ${list.length} clip(s) …`)
    type Row = { key: string; voice: string; engine: string; file: string; text: string; denoise?: string; tempo?: number; before?: Loudness; gain?: number; limit?: boolean; keep?: boolean }
    const rows: Row[] = []
    let next = 0
    await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 4 }, async () => {
      while (next < list.length) {
        const c = list[next++]
        const path = join(store.filesDir, c.file)
        const pre = c.engine === 'elevenlabs' && !c.denoise ? voices[c.voice] : undefined
        const pace = c.engine === 'gepard' && factor && c.tempo !== factor.tempo ? { tempo: Math.round((factor.tempo / (c.tempo ?? 1)) * 10_000) / 10_000, pause: factor.pause } : undefined
        const m = measure && FILE.test(c.file) && existsSync(path) ? await measure(new Uint8Array(readFileSync(path)), { denoise: pre, pace }) : null
        const g = m ? levelGain(m, { ...LEVEL, target }) : undefined
        rows.push({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, engine: c.engine, file: c.file, text: c.text, ...(pre ? { denoise: pre } : {}), ...(pace ? { tempo: pace.tempo } : {}), ...(m && g ? { before: m, gain: g.gain, limit: g.limit, keep: g.keep && !pre && !pace } : {}) })
      }
    }))
    const q = (xs: number[], f: number) => {
      const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b)
      return s.length ? s[Math.min(s.length - 1, Math.floor(f * (s.length - 1) + 0.5))] : NaN
    }
    const by = new Map<string, Row[]>()
    for (const r of rows) by.set(`${r.voice} ${r.engine}`, [...(by.get(`${r.voice} ${r.engine}`) ?? []), r])
    const groups = [...by].map(([name, g]) => {
      const m = g.filter(r => r.before && r.before.lufs > -70)
      const lufs = m.map(r => r.before!.lufs)
      const gains = m.map(r => r.gain!)
      // how far over the limiter's threshold the gain alone would take the limited clips' true peaks: what it holds back
      const limited = m.filter(r => r.limit && !r.keep)
      return {
        name, clips: g.length, measured: m.length,
        lufs: { median: q(lufs, 0.5), p10: q(lufs, 0.1), p90: q(lufs, 0.9) },
        gain: { median: q(gains, 0.5), min: Math.min(...gains), max: Math.max(...gains) },
        kept: g.filter(r => r.keep).length, limited: limited.length, over: q(limited.map(r => r.before!.peak + r.gain! - (LEVEL.peak - LIMIT_MARGIN)), 0.5), denoise: g.filter(r => r.denoise).length, paced: g.filter(r => r.tempo).length,
      }
    }).sort((a, b) => b.lufs.median - a.lufs.median)
    const summary = { target, peak: LEVEL.peak, waiting: queue.length, measured: rows.filter(r => r.before).length, ffmpeg: !!measure, dir: store.dir }
    if (flag('--json')) {
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, voices: Object.fromEntries(groups.map(({ name, ...g }) => [name, g])), clips: rows }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    const f1 = (x: number) => (Number.isFinite(x) ? `${x > 0 ? '+' : ''}${x.toFixed(1)}` : '—').padStart(6)
    console.log(`The level: ${target} LUFS integrated, true peak at most ${LEVEL.peak} dBTP. Clips in ${store.dir} not at it: ${queue.length}${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (groups.length) {
      console.log(`\n${'voice'.padEnd(22)} clips  LUFS now (p10 … p90)       gain (min … max)        kept  limited (over by)  filtered too  paced too`)
      for (const g of groups) {
        const lim = g.limited ? `${g.limited} (${g.over.toFixed(1)} dB)` : '0'
        console.log(`${g.name.padEnd(22)} ${String(g.clips).padStart(5)}  ${f1(g.lufs.median)} (${f1(g.lufs.p10)} … ${f1(g.lufs.p90)})  ${f1(g.gain.median)} (${f1(g.gain.min)} … ${f1(g.gain.max)})  ${String(g.kept).padStart(5)}  ${lim.padStart(17)}  ${String(g.denoise).padStart(12)}  ${String(g.paced).padStart(9)}`)
      }
      console.log(`(limited: the clips whose true peak the gain would take over ${LEVEL.peak - LIMIT_MARGIN} dB, where the limiter holds it, and by how much, the median)`)
      const unmeasured = rows.filter(r => !r.before).length
      if (unmeasured) console.log(`(${unmeasured} clip(s) not measured: no file, or ffmpeg failed)`)
    }
    if (!queue.length) process.exit(0)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each clip would get the gain (about 0.4 dB more where it is encoded again: the MP3 encode takes that off),`)
    console.log(`the limiter where its true peak would pass ${LEVEL.peak} dBTP, its voice's filter and a local clip's pace where they are due, in one encode; a clip within ${LEVEL.tolerance} dB`)
    console.log(`of the target keeps its file. The others are stored under a new file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded.`)
    console.log(`Level with: companion/bin/voice-build --level --run${tail}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegLeveller()) {
    console.error('voice-build --level: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Levelling ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s) to ${target} LUFS …`)
  const r = await store.levelClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nLevelled ${r.done} clip(s) (${r.kept} kept as they were, ${r.limited} limited)${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done > r.kept) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (edges) {
  // the silence at every clip's edges: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const queue = store.edgesQueue()
  const tail = `${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  const what = `${EDGES.lead} s kept before the sound, ${EDGES.tail} s after it (sound: over ${EDGES.threshold} dBFS in 20 ms, back and on while over ${EDGES.floor})`
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    // each clip measured as its file is (they are at the level): nothing is written
    const measure = ffmpegFileEdges()
    if (!measure) console.error('voice-build --edges: no ffmpeg here (LANI_FFMPEG names one): nothing measured')
    const list = queue.slice(0, max)
    if (measure && list.length) console.error(`Measuring ${list.length} clip(s) …`)
    type Row = { key: string; voice: string; engine: string; method?: string | null; text: string; edges?: Edges; trim?: boolean }
    const rows: Row[] = []
    let next = 0
    await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 8 }, async () => {
      while (next < list.length) {
        const c = list[next++]
        const path = join(store.filesDir, c.file)
        const e = measure && FILE.test(c.file) && existsSync(path) ? await measure(path) : null
        rows.push({ key: c.key, voice: c.voice, engine: c.engine, method: c.method ?? null, text: c.text, ...(e ? { edges: e, trim: trimmable(e, true) } : {}) })
      }
    }))
    const q = (xs: number[], f: number) => {
      const v = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b)
      return v.length ? v[Math.min(v.length - 1, Math.floor(f * (v.length - 1) + 0.5))] : NaN
    }
    // after: a trimmed clip's silence down to EDGES; the others' as it is
    const after = (r: Row) => (r.trim ? { lead: Math.min(r.edges!.lead, EDGES.lead), tail: Math.min(r.edges!.tail, EDGES.tail) } : r.edges!)
    const groupOf = (r: Row) => `${r.engine}${r.method === 'carrier' ? ' carrier' : ''}`
    const by = new Map<string, Row[]>()
    for (const r of rows) by.set(groupOf(r), [...(by.get(groupOf(r)) ?? []), r])
    const group = (name: string, g: Row[]) => {
      const m = g.filter(r => r.edges)
      const st = (xs: number[]) => ({ median: q(xs, 0.5), p90: q(xs, 0.9) })
      return {
        name, clips: g.length, measured: m.length, trim: m.filter(r => r.trim).length,
        lead: { now: st(m.map(r => r.edges!.lead)), after: st(m.map(r => after(r).lead)) },
        tail: { now: st(m.map(r => r.edges!.tail)), after: st(m.map(r => after(r).tail)) },
        seconds: m.reduce((n, r) => n + r.edges!.lead - after(r).lead + r.edges!.tail - after(r).tail, 0),
      }
    }
    const groups = [...[...by].map(([n, g]) => group(n, g)).sort((a, b) => b.clips - a.clips), ...(by.size > 1 ? [group('all', rows)] : [])]
    const summary = { edges: EDGES, waiting: queue.length, measured: rows.filter(r => r.edges).length, trim: rows.filter(r => r.trim).length, ffmpeg: !!measure, dir: store.dir }
    if (flag('--json')) {
      // and how many have more than 0.15 s at either edge (October 2026's measure)
      const over = (g: Row[]) => g.filter(r => r.edges && (r.edges.lead > 0.15 || r.edges.tail > 0.15)).length
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, over_015: Object.fromEntries([...by].map(([n, g]) => [n, over(g)])), groups: Object.fromEntries(groups.map(({ name, ...g }) => [name, g])), clips: rows }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    const f2 = (x: number) => (Number.isFinite(x) ? x.toFixed(2) : '—')
    console.log(`The edges: ${what}.`)
    console.log(`Clips in ${store.dir} not through it yet: ${queue.length}${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (groups.length && measure) {
      console.log(`\n${'engine'.padEnd(20)} clips   to trim  before: now (p90) → after     after: now (p90) → after    trimmed`)
      for (const g of groups) {
        console.log(`${g.name.padEnd(20)} ${String(g.clips).padStart(5)}  ${String(g.trim).padStart(10)}  ${`${f2(g.lead.now.median)} (${f2(g.lead.now.p90)}) → ${f2(g.lead.after.median)} (${f2(g.lead.after.p90)})`.padEnd(26)}  ${`${f2(g.tail.now.median)} (${f2(g.tail.now.p90)}) → ${f2(g.tail.after.median)} (${f2(g.tail.after.p90)})`.padEnd(26)} ${(g.seconds / 60).toFixed(1)} min`)
      }
      console.log(`(before / after: the silence before and after the sound, seconds, the median and p90; to trim: the clips with more than ${EDGES.slack.lead} s before it or ${EDGES.slack.tail} s after it)`)
      const unmeasured = rows.filter(r => !r.edges).length
      if (unmeasured) console.log(`(${unmeasured} clip(s) not measured: no file, or ffmpeg failed)`)
    }
    if (!queue.length) process.exit(0)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. The clips to trim are trimmed and brought to the level again in one encode, each under a new`)
    console.log('file name, the old file removed once the new one is recorded; the others are only recorded. No engine is asked, no characters spent.')
    console.log(`Trim with: companion/bin/voice-build --edges --run${tail}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegLeveller()) {
    console.error('voice-build --edges: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Through the edges: ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} clip(s): ${what} …`)
  const r = await store.edgesClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\n${r.done} clip(s) done: ${r.trimmed} trimmed, ${r.kept} kept as they were${r.limited ? `, ${r.limited} limited` : ''}${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done > r.kept) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (restore) {
  // the local clips paced before, back from a snapshot: no engine, no ffmpeg
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const run = flag('--run')
  const quiet = flag('--json')
  console.error(`The local clips paced before (tempo set) in ${store.dir}, from ${snapshot} …`)
  const r = store.restorePaced(snapshot!, { run, max, out: quiet ? undefined : line => console.log(line) })
  if (quiet) console.log(JSON.stringify(r, null, 2))
  else {
    console.log(`\nPaced local clips: ${r.paced}. ${run ? 'Restored' : 'To restore'}: ${r.restored}${run ? ` (${r.verified} byte for byte the snapshot's file)` : ''}; not restorable: ${r.missing.length}${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} changed meanwhile` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; still paced: ${r.left}.`)
    if (!run && r.restored) console.log(`Dry run: nothing changed. Restore with: companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard ${snapshotArg} --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    if (run && r.restored) console.log('Then trim their edges: companion/bin/voice-build --edges --run. A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated).')
  }
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
if (tempo) {
  // the local voice's pace: ffmpeg only, the corpus and the engines aren't needed
  const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
  const set = store.pace
  if (!set) {
    const st = store.tempoStats()
    console.log("The local voice keeps its own pace (no LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_TEMPO or LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_PAUSES): nothing to pace.")
    if (st.paced) console.log(`${st.paced} local clip(s) were paced before: back with companion/bin/voice-build --restore-gepard <a snapshot from before>, then --edges.`)
    console.log('Their silence at the edges is trimmed as every clip\'s: companion/bin/voice-build --edges.')
    process.exit(0)
  }
  const factor = set.tempo
  const queue = store.tempoQueue()
  const chars = queue.reduce((n, c) => n + c.text.trim().length, 0)
  const tail = `${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`
  const what = `${set.pause ? `pauses over ${set.pause} s down to it (LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_PAUSES), ` : ''}${factor !== 1 ? `sped up ×${factor} (LANI_VOICE_GEPARD_TEMPO), the pitch kept, ` : ''}the edges trimmed`
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    const pace = ffmpegPace()
    if (!pace) console.error('voice-build --tempo: no ffmpeg here (LANI_FFMPEG names one): nothing measured')
    const list = queue.slice(0, max)
    // characters a second on texts of 15 to 80 characters (a lone word is mostly its edges)
    const sentence = (t: string) => t.trim().length >= 15 && t.trim().length <= 80
    const q = (xs: number[], f: number) => {
      const s = [...xs].sort((a, b) => a - b)
      return s.length ? s[Math.min(s.length - 1, Math.floor(f * (s.length - 1) + 0.5))] : NaN
    }
    const stat = (xs: number[]) => ({ median: q(xs, 0.5), p10: q(xs, 0.1), p90: q(xs, 0.9), n: xs.length })
    // [n] clips spread over [all] (the same ones every time)
    const spread = <T,>(all: T[], n: number) => (all.length <= n ? all : Array.from({ length: n }, (_, i) => all[Math.floor((i * all.length) / n)]))
    const measureAll = async <T extends { file: string },>(xs: T[], af: (x: T) => string | undefined) => {
      const out: (T & { pace?: Pace; after?: Pace })[] = []
      let next = 0
      await Promise.all(Array.from({ length: 4 }, async () => {
        while (next < xs.length) {
          const x = xs[next++]
          const path = join(store.filesDir, x.file)
          const bytes = pace && FILE.test(x.file) && existsSync(path) ? new Uint8Array(readFileSync(path)) : undefined
          const now = bytes ? await pace!(bytes) : null
          const chain = af(x)
          const after = bytes && chain ? await pace!(bytes, chain) : null
          out.push({ ...x, ...(now ? { pace: now } : {}), ...(after ? { after } : {}) })
        }
      }))
      return out
    }
    if (list.length && pace) console.error(`Measuring ${list.length} clip(s) …`)
    const rows = await measureAll(list, c => paceChain({ tempo: Math.round((factor / (c.tempo ?? 1)) * 10_000) / 10_000, pause: set.pause }) || undefined)
    // the reference: ElevenLabs' clips of the same voices; and the local clips paced already, as they are now
    const local = [...new Set(store.database.query("SELECT DISTINCT voice FROM clips WHERE engine = 'gepard'").all().map(r => (r as { voice: string }).voice))]
    const ofVoices = (engine: string) => (store.database.query(`SELECT * FROM clips WHERE engine = ? AND voice IN (${local.map(() => '?').join(', ') || "''"}) ORDER BY key`).all(engine, ...local) as Clip[]).filter(c => sentence(c.text))
    const eleven = pace ? await measureAll(spread(ofVoices('elevenlabs'), 120), () => undefined) : []
    const done = pace ? await measureAll(spread(ofVoices('gepard').filter(c => c.tempo === factor), 120), () => undefined) : []
    const rate = (xs: { text: string; pace?: Pace }[], k: 'pace' | 'after' = 'pace') =>
      stat(xs.filter(x => sentence(x.text) && (x as Record<string, unknown>)[k]).map(x => charsPerSecond(x.text, ((x as Record<string, unknown>)[k] as Pace).secs)))
    const by = new Map<string, typeof rows>()
    for (const r of rows) by.set(r.voice, [...(by.get(r.voice) ?? []), r])
    const group = (name: string, g: typeof rows) => {
      const m = g.filter(r => r.pace && r.after)
      const sum = (k: 'pace' | 'after') => m.reduce((n, r) => n + r[k]!.secs, 0)
      return {
        name, clips: g.length, measured: m.length,
        rate: { now: rate(m), after: rate(m, 'after') },
        edges: { now: stat(m.map(r => r.pace!.lead + r.pace!.tail)).median, after: stat(m.map(r => r.after!.lead + r.after!.tail)).median },
        paused: { now: stat(m.map(r => r.pace!.paused)).median, after: stat(m.map(r => r.after!.paused)).median },
        seconds: { now: sum('pace'), after: sum('after') },
      }
    }
    const groups = [...[...by].map(([v, g]) => group(`${v} gepard`, g)).sort((a, b) => b.clips - a.clips), ...(by.size > 1 ? [group('all', rows)] : [])]
    const summary = { tempo: factor, pace: set, waiting: queue.length, chars, measured: rows.filter(r => r.after).length, ffmpeg: !!pace, dir: store.dir, elevenlabs: rate(eleven), paced: rate(done) }
    if (flag('--json')) {
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ ...summary, voices: Object.fromEntries(groups.map(({ name, ...g }) => [name, g])), clips: rows.map(({ key, voice, file, text, tempo, pace, after }) => ({ key, voice, file, text, tempo, now: pace, after })) }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    const f1 = (x: number, w = 5) => (Number.isFinite(x) ? x.toFixed(1) : '—').padStart(w)
    const r3 = (s: { median: number; p10: number; p90: number }) => `${f1(s.median)} (${f1(s.p10, 4)} … ${f1(s.p90, 4)})`
    console.log(`The local voice's pace: ${what}.`)
    console.log(`Local clips in ${store.dir} not at it: ${queue.length} (${chars} characters)${max !== undefined && max < queue.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (groups.length && pace) {
      console.log(`\n${'voice'.padEnd(16)} clips  chars/s now (p10 … p90)   paced (p10 … p90)     edges now → paced   pauses now → paced   length now → paced`)
      for (const g of groups) {
        const edges = `${g.edges.now.toFixed(2)} → ${g.edges.after.toFixed(2)} s`
        const pauses = `${g.paused.now.toFixed(2)} → ${g.paused.after.toFixed(2)} s`
        console.log(`${g.name.padEnd(16)} ${String(g.clips).padStart(5)}  ${r3(g.rate.now)}    ${r3(g.rate.after)}  ${edges.padStart(17)}   ${pauses.padStart(18)}   ${(g.seconds.now / 60).toFixed(1)} → ${(g.seconds.after / 60).toFixed(1)} min`)
      }
      console.log('(chars/s: the medians of texts of 15 to 80 characters; edges: the silence before and after the sound, pauses: of 0.1 s or more in all; the medians a clip)')
      const unmeasured = rows.filter(r => !r.after).length
      if (unmeasured) console.log(`(${unmeasured} clip(s) not measured: no file, or ffmpeg failed)`)
    }
    if (pace && summary.elevenlabs.n) console.log(`\nElevenLabs, the same voices (${summary.elevenlabs.n} clips of 15 to 80 characters): ${r3(summary.elevenlabs)} chars/s`)
    if (pace && summary.paced.n) console.log(`Local clips paced already (×${factor}; ${summary.paced.n} of 15 to 80 characters): ${r3(summary.paced)} chars/s`)
    if (!queue.length) process.exit(0)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each clip would be paced and brought to the level again in one encode, under a new file name, the`)
    console.log('old file removed once the new one is recorded. No engine is asked, no characters spent.')
    console.log(`Pace with: companion/bin/voice-build --tempo --run${tail}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!ffmpegLeveller()) {
    console.error('voice-build --tempo: no ffmpeg (LANI_FFMPEG names one)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Pacing ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, queue.length) : queue.length} of ${queue.length} local clip(s): ${what} …`)
  const r = await store.tempoClips({ max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nPaced ${r.done} clip(s)${r.limited ? ` (${r.limited} limited)` : ''}${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} skipped (no file, or made again meanwhile)` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} waiting.`)
  if (r.done) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed ? 1 : 0)
}
const packs =new PackStore(packsDirs(process.env.LANI_PACKS_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/packs'), cultures, culture, language), join(appDir, 'packs'))
const modules = new ModuleStore(join(appDir, 'modules'), ofLanguage(process.env.LANI_MODULES_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/modules')), log)
const scenarios = new ScenarioStore(ofLanguage(process.env.LANI_SCENARIOS_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/scenarios')), join(appDir, 'scenarios'))
const villagers = new VillagerStore(process.env.LANI_VILLAGERS_DIR ?? join(cultureDir(cultures, culture), 'villagers'), join(appDir, 'villagers'), log)
const scenes = new SceneStore(scenesDirs(process.env.LANI_SCENES_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/scenes'), cultures, culture, language), join(appDir, 'scenes'), () => ({ packs: packs.all(), scenarios: scenarios.all(), villagers: villagers.all() }), log)
// the storyteller's stories: the village's culture pack's (its stories/), and the tutor's, as the bridge has them
const stories = new StoryStore(storiesDirs(cultures, culture), join(appDir, 'stories'), () => ({ packs: packs.all(), villagers: villagers.all() }), log)
// the car's audio drills of the village's language (companion/drills/<language>), as the bridge has them
const drills = new DrillStore(drillsDir(process.env.LANI_DRILLS_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/drills'), language), language, () => ({ packs: packs.all(), villagers: villagers.all() }), log)
// the grammar book of the village's language and the tutor's pages: their examples, as the bridge has them
const grammar = new GrammarStore(grammarDir(process.env.LANI_GRAMMAR_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/grammar'), language), language, join(appDir, 'grammar'), log)

const { eleven, gepard } = enginesFromEnv(process.env, log, language)
// the local worker speaks only Slovene; a culture's cast without voices yet voices nothing (the phone's TTS speaks)
const store = new VoiceStore({ appDir, dir: voiceDir(appDir), engines: language === 'sl' ? [eleven, gepard] : castVoiced() ? [eleven] : [], log, readonly: !flag('--run'), ...villageVoices })
// the voices of their own that are ready (the voice profiles, in the store's database): a storyteller who has one tells
// in it ("@janez", as the app asks for it by the fire), and ElevenLabs makes those clips in it
const own = ownVoicesIn(store.database)
usePersonVoices(id => own.get(id))
const items = corpus({
  packs: packs.all(),
  modules: modules.list().filter(m => !m.tags.includes('retired')).flatMap(m => modules.get(m.id) ?? []),
  scenarios: scenarios.all(),
  scenes: scenes.resolved(),
  // the culture's keepers' talks (world.json `spots`: the charcoal burner's meeting and his story, every telling)
  keepers: cultureKeepers(cultures, culture).map(k => ({ ...k, tellings: keeperTellings(k) })),
  // the village projects' steps as short scenes (project-steps/: every telling, each line in its speaker's voice)
  steps: cultureStepFiles(cultures, culture).map(f => ({ project: f.project, tellings: stepTellings(f) })),
  villagers: villagers.all(),
  stories: stories.all(),
  drills: drills.all(),
  grammar: grammar.all(),
  // «Vidim, vidim»: what a child says playing I spy in the scenes (companion/ispy, the app bundles it)
  ispy: readISpy(process.env.LANI_ISPY_DIR ?? join(root, 'companion/ispy')),
  ownVoice: id => !!personVoice(`@${id}`),
  cards: (() => {
    const sr = join(appDir, '..', 'spaced-repetition.json')
    return existsSync(sr) ? cardTexts(JSON.parse(readFileSync(sr, 'utf8')).items ?? {}) : []
  })(),
  language,
  // rendered for the learner ({learner}, {m:…|f:…}: addressee.ts), as the app says it
  learner: addresseeOf(join(appDir, '..'), language),
})

if (narrators) {
  // the narrators' Slovene clips in their local voice: the corpus tells which are Slovene, no ElevenLabs
  if (!villageVoices.localNarrators) {
    console.log(language !== 'sl' ? `The narrators of this village (${language}) speak as its voice cast has them: nothing to do.` : 'LANI_VOICE_NARRATOR_SL=elevenlabs: the narrators speak with their ElevenLabs voices: nothing to do.')
    process.exit(0)
  }
  // Slovene: a clip of this village's corpus, of a source the corpus has, or a line the app spoke here
  const keys = new Set(items.map(i => clipKey(normalizeText(i.text), i.voice)))
  const sources = new Set(items.map(i => i.source))
  const spoken = new Set(['live', 'road'])
  const slovene = (c: Clip) => keys.has(c.key) || sources.has(c.source) || spoken.has(c.source)
  const { todo, skipped } = store.narratorQueue(slovene)
  const count = (xs: Clip[]) => {
    const by: Record<string, number> = {}
    for (const c of xs) {
      const k = `${c.voice} ${c.engine}${c.method === 'carrier' ? ' carrier' : ''}${c.engine === 'gepard' ? ` (${c.engine_voice ?? 'ana'})` : ''}`
      by[k] = (by[k] ?? 0) + 1
    }
    return by
  }
  const up = await gepard.up()
  const voices = { female: store.localVoiceOf('female'), male: store.localVoiceOf('male') }
  if (!flag('--run')) {
    if (flag('--json')) {
      console.log(JSON.stringify({ voices, todo: todo.length, chars: todo.reduce((n, c) => n + c.text.length, 0), by: count(todo), skipped: skipped.map(c => ({ key: c.key, source: c.source, engine: c.engine, text: c.text })), gepard_up: up, dir: store.dir }, null, 2))
      process.exit(0)
    }
    console.log(`The narrators' local voices: female ${voices.female}, male ${voices.male}. Their clips in ${store.dir} not in them yet: ${todo.length + skipped.length}`)
    for (const [k, n] of Object.entries(count(todo)).sort((a, b) => b[1] - a[1])) console.log(`  ${k.padEnd(32)} ${String(n).padStart(5)}`)
    console.log(`Slovene, to make again: ${todo.length} (${todo.reduce((n, c) => n + c.text.length, 0)} characters; about ${Math.ceil(todo.length / 60)} minutes at a second a clip)${max !== undefined && max < todo.length ? `; this run: ${max}` : ''}`)
    if (skipped.length) {
      console.log(`Left as they are, not known to be Slovene (not in this village's corpus, its sources, or spoken here): ${skipped.length}`)
      for (const c of skipped) console.log(`  · ${c.voice.padEnd(7)} ${c.source.padEnd(24)} ${c.text.length > 60 ? `${c.text.slice(0, 59)}…` : c.text}`)
    }
    console.log(`Local Gepard worker: ${up ? 'up' : 'down (the run needs it)'}`)
    console.log(`\nDry run: nothing changed. Each is made again by the local worker, its edges trimmed and levelled, under a new file name, the old`)
    console.log('file removed once the new one is recorded. No ElevenLabs. The run can stop any time: the next one goes on where it stopped.')
    console.log(`Re-voice with: companion/bin/voice-build --narrators --run${max !== undefined ? ` --max ${max}` : ''}${data ? ` --data ${data}` : ''}`)
    process.exit(0)
  }
  if (!up) {
    console.error('voice-build --narrators: the local Gepard worker is down (LANI_GEPARD_URL)')
    process.exit(1)
  }
  console.log(`Re-voicing ${max !== undefined ? Math.min(max, todo.length) : todo.length} of ${todo.length} narrator clip(s) in the local voice (female ${voices.female}, male ${voices.male}) …`)
  const r = await store.revoiceNarrators(slovene, { max, out: line => console.log(line) })
  console.log(`\nMade ${r.made} again in the local voice${r.skipped ? `; ${r.skipped} changed meanwhile` : ''}${r.failed ? `; ${r.failed} failed` : ''}; ${r.left} left${r.stopped ? ` (stopped: ${r.stopped})` : ''}.`)
  if (r.made) console.log('A running bridge tells the app within a minute (voice_updated); the app downloads the new files as it plays them.')
  if (flag('--json')) console.log(JSON.stringify(r))
  store.close()
  process.exit(r.failed || r.stopped ? 1 : 0)
}

